#. gauge shotgun"
#. ~ Description of variant "S&R Ranger 12 gauge shotgun" of item "double-
#. barreled shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/shot.json
msgid ""
"An antique double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  These were made by"
" many different manufacturers, but these inexpensive firearms were all sold "
"in the Sears and Roebuck catalog in the days of yore."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "double-barreled shotgun"
#. ~ Variant name of item "double-barreled shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/shot.json
msgid "Parker Bros. Trojan 12 gauge shotgun"
msgid_plural "Parker Bros. Trojan 12 gauge shotguns"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "double-barreled shotgun" of gun "Parker Bros.
#. Trojan 12 gauge shotgun"
#. ~ Description of variant "Parker Bros. Trojan 12 gauge shotgun" of item
#. "double-barreled shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/shot.json
msgid ""
"An antique double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  Not to be confused"
" with the board game company of the same name, Parker Bros. made shotguns "
"from 1867 to 1942, before they were phased out of production by Remington, "
"who had acquired the company the previous decade.  These shotguns were sold "
"in many different \"grades\" at varying price points, with higher quality of "
"engravings being included at higher cost.  This particular shotgun is a "
"\"Trojan\", which was the cheapest grade Parker Bros. sold."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "double-barreled shotgun"
#. ~ Variant name of item "double-barreled shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/shot.json
msgid "CZ Bobwhite 12 gauge shotgun"
msgid_plural "CZ Bobwhite 12 gauge shotguns"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "double-barreled shotgun" of gun "CZ Bobwhite 12
#. gauge shotgun"
#. ~ Description of variant "CZ Bobwhite 12 gauge shotgun" of item "double-
#. barreled shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/shot.json
msgid ""
"A relatively modern double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  \"CZ\" "
"stands for \"Česká zbrojovka\", or Czech armory.  CZ's weapons are either "
"Czech imports or produced by their US based subsidiaries.  This specific "
"model is the Bobwhite, with a wooden stock and black chrome barrels."
msgstr ""

